  "reply_text": "*Found one merge-blocking bug.*\n\n* [P1] View-only shares can edit unlocked documents — `src/guard.js:12`\n  `share.mask & WRITE === WRITE` is parsed as `share.mask & (WRITE === WRITE)`, effectively checking bit `1` (`READ`) rather than `WRITE`. As a result, `canEdit({ mask: READ, locked: false })` returns `true`. Conversely, a WRITE-only share is denied editing.\n\n  Suggested correction: use `hasRight(share.mask, WRITE) && !share.locked`. Add regression tests for an unlocked READ-only share being denied and a WRITE-only share being allowed.\n\nAll six existing tests pass, but they miss this because the editor fixture includes both READ and WRITE. I also checked all 16 permission masks in locked/unlocked states, toggle behavior, and transfers between distinct users; no other issues found in those checks.\n\nNo code or files changed.",
